  "plain_language": [
    "Quota q = 20% (1 of the 5 slots). It costs 0.014 NDCG@5 (95% range 0.010 to 0.019; 2.7%) and raises the share of slots for new or small groups from 2% to 20%; 126 groups are shown instead of 108, and the Gini of exposure falls from 0.66 to 0.52. It serves equity and inclusion (R4): a new or small group cannot gain members if nobody sees it.",
    "Global cap c = 5%. On personalised lists it changes nothing: no group reaches 5% of the slots there (at most 4.7% in any setting). On the default list, where every member sees nearly the same groups, it costs nothing: NDCG@5 even rises by 0.040 (95% range 0.028 to 0.051) and shows 23 groups instead of 8; the most-shown group falls from 20% to 5% of the slots. It serves equity (R4): no group takes everyone's attention.",
    "Topic cap n = 2. It costs 0.001 NDCG@5 (95% range -0.001 to 0.003; 0.2%) and raises the hidden topics in a list of 5 from 2.52 to 2.59. It serves diversity and autonomy (R5): a list that is not all one subject leaves the member a real choice.",
    "Variety weight λ = 0.8. It costs 0.002 NDCG@5 (95% range -0.002 to 0.007; 0.5%) and raises the topics in a list from 2.40 to 2.59 (description diversity 0.922 to 0.949). It serves diversity (R5): groups unlike each other in a list.",
    "Together, the four dials cost 0.015 NDCG@5 against the hybrid without re-ranking (2.8% of its 0.541; 95% range 0.010 to 0.020), within the 5% budget chosen on the practice quiz, and members still find a hidden group in 65% of lists (today's BOING: 22%)."
  ]
